{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqend24x8gj","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"handoff task result validation gating on overlay status","summary":"Daemon-side validation of structured task_result on terminal completion (POST /overlay/status, MCP complete_task) is gated two ways to preserve back-compat: (1) opt-in — only enforced when the caller sends a structured `task_result` object; legacy free-string `summary`-only complete_task passes through untouched (MCP complete_task today sends no task_result, so legacy is unaffected). (2) scoped — the single invariant enforced is metric-result completeness: a task carrying a metric spec (overlay.metrics[key], the has_metric_spec discriminator) must report task_result.metric_measurements, else 409. Non-metric tasks are never refused. Refusal placed right before setStatus mutation, after the existing in_progress metric-branch 409, reusing that invariant's shape (no new mechanism, no hook). Note: metric MEASUREMENTS still live separately on the node via measure_task → overlay.measurement; this gate only checks the worker SELF-REPORTED them in the handoff envelope.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T03:21:57.777Z","vec":[-0.0736343041062355,0.02639094553887844,0.007174708414822817,-0.011044032871723175,0.04733347147703171,-0.0630575567483902,0.01515360176563263,0.00044787381193600595,-0.0027483212761580944,-0.01445108000189066,-0.0012985467910766602,-0.009503942914307117,0.018122360110282898,0.0263360608369112,-0.0489494614303112,-0.059672098606824875,0.15074871480464935,-0.041229650378227234,0.022544367238879204,-0.039301637560129166,0.049028292298316956,0.015760283917188644,0.05136444419622421,0.05991845205426216,-0.0664282962679863,-0.05075611546635628,-0.11909577995538712,-0.03486987575888634,0.0022578223142772913,-0.005637431517243385,-0.04808826372027397,0.07998182624578476,-0.010997026227414608,0.002850200282409787,0.004133704584091902,0.13525035977363586,0.05592648684978485,-0.03596335276961